        "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14096165/assets/89fa15ffb9a7f6b319cf3b9ff0de4ab821a15f632d7f93618fbe99b7979260f4.png)\n\nDescribe the set of points shown above using set-builder notation.",
        "worked_solution": "Since all points $P(x,y)$ in our set lie at integer values of $x$ and $y,$ we have $x\\in \\mathbb Z, y\\in\\mathbb Z,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in \\mathbb Z\\times\\mathbb Z = \\mathbb Z^2.\n$$\n\nThe points $P(x,y)$ satisfy the condition\n\n$$\nx \\in \\{1,2,3\\}, \\quad y \\in \\{ -3,-2,-1,0,1,2 \\}.\n$$\n\nIn other words,\n\n$$\n1 \\leq x \\leq 3, \\quad -3 \\leq y \\leq 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\n\\Big\\{ (x,y)  \\in \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\mathbb Z^2}\n\\: : \\: \n\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}1}  \n\\leq  x \\leq  \n\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}3} , \\: \n\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-3}  \n\\leq  y \\leq  \n\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}2} \n\\Big\\}.\n$$",
        "screenshot": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14096165/example-13145.png"
      }
    ],
